{"parentUuid":"bf10fd81-a2fd-49a2-98e6-9135ce5e01c7","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"677e2e7b-6923-4566-b71d-c472bcf45181","agentId":"a09009e70701a4229","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LPe9WtxzJkq9ZMx1JfgWgP","type":"tool_result","content":"all 6 checks passed","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"cc07db5c-b3db-4d5b-ba23-32684db6fde0","timestamp":"2026-10-14T16:37:29.193Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"all 6 checks passed","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\docs\\handbook\\02-architecture.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":179,"oldLines":6,"newStart":179,"newLines":70,"lines":[" "," Verification: `verify_repair`."," ","+## Connect to car flow (2026-10-14)","+","+**Client**: `cuore/web/static/connect.js` (progressive enhancement overlay on the plain `/v/{vin}/scans` link in `_vbar.html`'s `#connect-drawer`). Never runs on page load; only a real tap on `#connect-car-btn` starts anything. Each refusal is shown with the live layer's real error text (from `cuore/live/ops.py`/`cuore/live/transport.py`), never invented copy.","+","+**Server**: `POST /api/live/connect/start` (`cuore/api/live.py`) -- the one additive route -- runs pre-checks in order (adapter found → bus verified → VIN matches) and, if every one passes, starts or reports an already-open guided scan (`cuore/live/fullscan.py`). Every pause after that reuses the existing `/api/live/fullscan/guided/continue`, `/skip` endpoints.","+","+## Modifications layer (2026-10-14 NO-GO decision)","+","+**Rule**: CUORE diagnoses, it never performs coding/configuration writes itself. A modification is done in MES/wiTECH via a handoff card (below) and RECORDED here with who/when/from→to/backup/verification.","+","+**Catalogue** (read-only): `mes/modifications.py` -- known modifications seeded from `mes.mes_functions` (rows of kind `\"coding\"`/`\"adjustment\"`) and a paddle-shift research pass (2026-10-14). Same split as `mes.parts` and `mes.mechanic_tests`: \"what we know about this kind of thing.\"","+","+**Ledger** (writable): `cuore/live/modifications.py` (append-only JSONL, `modifications.jsonl`) -- one car's actual edits, stamped with who/when/from/to/backup/verification. Four record shapes: `record`, `delete`, `restore`, `amend` (soft deletes + undos, folded in append order).","+","+**Routes**: `cuore/web/mods_routes.py` (HTML `/v/{vin}/mods`, `/v/{vin}/mods/{mod_id}`), `cuore/api/modifications.py` (`/api/mods/catalog*`, `/api/mods/{vin}*`). The catalogue is generated from a research pass, not user-edited; the ledger is writable via `cuore/services/modifications_bridge.py`.","+","+## MES handoff cards (2026-10-14)","+","+**What**: when CUORE diagnoses that a coding/adjustment/actuator command is needed, it hands the technician a card -- module, menu path, prerequisites -- built from `mes.mes_functions`, never a cuore-driven write.","+","+**Module**: `cuore/services/mes_handoff_bridge.py`. Two functions: `:func:`candidates`/`:func:`card` (lookup matched against a test id or free-text step label) + `:func:`import_mes_log`/`:func:`list_mes_scans` (MES-captured logs outside cuore's live link get a health report via the same `mes.scan_health.verdict` without disguising them as live serial reads).","+","+**Import state**: `cuore/live/config.state_dir()` holds `mes_imports.json` (ledger of MES-sourced scans with verdicts), parallel to cuore's own `cuore/live/scanlog.py` (observations.jsonl) but never written to by the live layer.","+","+**UI**: `cuore/web/templates/_mes_handoff.html` (card template, embedded in Tests/Job pages).","+","+## CUORE log MCP tools (2026-10-14)","+","+**Scan tools** (`mes.cuore_log`, new module): `cuore_list_scans`, `cuore_latest_scan`, `cuore_read_scan`, `cuore_export_scan` -- read `CUORE_STATE_DIR`'s live-scan log (`cuore/live/scanlog.py`, observation clustering) identically to how MES tools read MultiEcuScan's files. Each scan tagged `full`/`guided`/`partial`/`attempt`.","+","+**Search tool**: `cuore_search` extends `search_logs`'s regex-with-context shape across `observations.jsonl`, `owner_events.jsonl`, `attested.jsonl`, `jobs.jsonl` and recording headers, read directly off disk (works even if `cuore.live` is not importable).","+","+**Timeline**: `logs_timeline(vin)` merges MES and CUORE lists into one newest-first, sourced view. `mes.catalog.LogEntry` now carries a `provenance` field; a second log root -- `CUORE_STATE_DIR/scans/<vin>/` where `cuore.live.scanlog.write_mes_export` writes MES-format exports -- is scanned alongside MES roots and tagged `provenance=\"cuore live export\"` (real from-car data, never flagged `simulation`).","+","+**Hygiene**: `cuore_log_dir` reports store-file sizes; `cuore_log_archive` copies a dated, sha256-manifested snapshot of every CUORE log file to `CUORE_STATE_DIR/archive/` without truncating originals; `cuore_log_integrity` parses every store line and reports counts per kind/op/day. Same search independently implemented over HTTP at `GET /api/scans/search` (`cuore/api/scanlog.py`).","+","+## Transmission additions (2026-10-14)","+","+**Label kind**: `cuore/web/owner_routes.py` adds a label kind mapping `(\"fluids\", \"driveline_fluid\")` → `(\"transmission_service\", \"\")` for \"Tell CUORE\" fill-up guidance.","+","+**Parts**: `mes/parts.py` includes `transmission_fluid` (ZF 8HP ATF, location/related jobs/torque keys).","+","+**MES recording channels**: drivetrain-specific channels exposed in live capture; TCM DID discovery (`discover_module_dids`) for transmission-module reads.","+","+## Others' experience inputs (2026-10-14)","+","+**Module**: `cuore/live/experience_inputs.py` (append-only JSONL, `experience_inputs.jsonl`) -- driver/mechanic finds (YouTube video, forum thread, photo, note) typed in today, attributed to finder, shown on the code-experience card at confidence `\"reported\"` (same posture as `owner_events` and `mes.symptoms`, a person's claim not a fact).","+","+**Four record shapes**: `input` (url, title, kind, found_by, verified status), `input_edit` (never rewrites original), `delete`/`restore` (soft delete + undo), `flag`/`worked` (marks on any link id, curated or user-added).","+","+**API**: `cuore/services/experience_inputs_bridge.py` + `cuore/api/experience.py` (HTTP face, via `/api/experience/*`).","+","+**Verification**: `:func:`verify_entry` (module-level, so tests monkeypatch it) uses a browser User-Agent GET for most hosts; XenForo forums (stelvioforum/giuliaforums/alfabb/alfaowner) sit behind JS challenge (202 to plain clients) so those are confirmed by headless Edge. Failure degrades to `{\"status\": \"unreachable\"}` rather than blocking save.","+","+## Safety gates in `cuore/live/safety.py`","+","+Three independent checks, all pure functions:","+","+- `:func:`validate_command` -- CR, LF, STN batch separator rejected so nothing smuggles a second command past the classifier.","+- `:func:`classify_command` -- `read` / `vehicle_write` / `adapter_state` / `blocked` with allowlists for AT (`AT_READ_ONLY`) and ST (`ST_READ_ONLY`) reads rather than deny-lists.","+- `:func:`assert_read_only_uds` / `:func:`assert_transmit_allowed` -- HTTP layer's guarantee of no write route; cable protocol's ban on 500 kbps onto 125 kbps bus.","+","+**Write services** (`WRITE_SERVICES` dict): UDS service codes that change vehicle state, e.g. `\"2E\"` (WriteDataByIdentifier, configuration), `\"2F\"` (InputOutputControl, actuates hardware), `\"31\"` (RoutineControl, adaptations/service routines).","+"," ## Launchers and keep-alive"," "," - `start-cuore.ps1` -- launches cuore if not already up and opens a page in the default browser (`-Page`, `-Restart`). Only stops a process whose command line is `python -m cuore`, so it never kills an unrelated server."]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\docs\\handbook\\02-architecture.md"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"af2a0e87-2309-4815-9276-24a31bdd974c","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","platform":"windows"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"bf10fd81-a2fd-49a2-98e6-9135ce5e01c7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
