{"parentUuid":"e10386f4-bdaf-4187-88b1-ee8b5672afc7","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a09009e70701a4229","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cg2TTq27A5nqhMpHB4uLu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PhJSWqdQwKZrMi1o7FKxJX","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd C:/Users/User/mcp-servers && .venv/Scripts/python.exe cuore/tests/check_bench.py 2>&1 | tail -40"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":356,"cache_read_input_tokens":134263,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":356,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01PhJSWqdQwKZrMi1o7FKxJX":{"command":"cd C:/Users/User/mcp-servers && .venv/Scripts/python.exe cuore/tests/check_bench.py 2>&1 | tail -40"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"7a6ba059-372f-468a-bd71-3f95d27311d7","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Cg2TTpkyTSGQmXTz4W7Pf","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"3cc4b032-c287-4023-b91d-58a9aefa46e8","timestamp":"2026-10-14T16:37:32.463Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"e10386f4-bdaf-4187-88b1-ee8b5672afc7","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"677e2e7b-6923-4566-b71d-c472bcf45181","agentId":"a09009e70701a4229","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Wt5RC6y5CEqiZFf54k2fMP","type":"tool_result","content":"=== overflow check at 400px (no screenshot) ===\r\n\r\nall 28 checks passed","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"2c1a6af3-685d-4f9f-988b-01069abe6abc","timestamp":"2026-10-14T16:37:56.681Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"=== overflow check at 400px (no screenshot) ===\r\n\r\nall 28 checks passed","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\docs\\handbook\\05-methods-and-gotchas.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":20,"oldLines":3,"newStart":20,"newLines":7,"lines":[" - Tell CUORE's phone URL moves with the PC's LAN address: cuore binds `CUORE_HOST=0.0.0.0` (set in the launchers) and the shop PC is on DHCP, so the IP in the `/m/{vin}/qr` URL (192.168.68.80 as of 2026-10-13; was 192.168.0.161) can change on a reboot or router restart -- check the current address before handing a phone the link, don't assume last session's. The Windows Firewall rule for inbound TCP 5000 needs an admin to run once (`New-NetFirewallRule -DisplayName \"CUORE 5000\" -Direction Inbound -Action Allow -Protocol TCP -LocalPort 5000 -Profile Any`); without it the LAN bind is correct but nothing outside the PC itself can reach the port."," - \"Read this photo\" (`POST /api/vision/{vin}/read`, `cuore/services/vision_bridge.py` + `cuore/api/vision.py`): a value read from a photo is a **suggestion the human confirms**, never a car measurement -- when the confirmed value is saved as an owner event, the caller stamps `fields_meta[key] = \"photo\"` on that field (same provenance convention `cuore.live.owner_events` already uses) so the record still says it came from a picture, not an instrument. Field names in the response are the real `cuore.live.owner_events.TAXONOMY` field names for the hints that map onto one kind (`fuel_pump` -> `fuel/fill_up`, `oil_bottle` -> `fluids/engine_oil_change`, `part_label` -> `parts_repairs_elsewhere/part_fitted_elsewhere`, `receipt` -> `fuel/fill_up`); `odometer` returns `odometer_km` with `suggested_kind: null` because that is the event's own top-level field, not a kind field. Provider is `CUORE_VISION_PROVIDER` (default `none`, which is deliberately the honest \"not set up, fill in by hand\" answer -- CUORE runs offline by rule, so a vision backend is never silently on). `claude` only turns on with `CUORE_VISION_PROVIDER=claude` **and** `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` set -- that call leaves the LAN and goes to Anthropic over plain HTTPS via `urllib` (no `anthropic` SDK in this venv, and none was added), so it is the owner's explicit, informed choice, never a default. `tesseract` is a probe-only stub (`_find_tesseract` checks PATH and `C:\\Program Files\\Tesseract-OCR\\tesseract.exe`); nothing is installed there today and no OCR is wired up behind it. Tests (`cuore/tests/check_vision.py`) monkeypatch `cuore.services.vision_bridge.urllib.request.urlopen` to return a canned Messages-API body rather than calling the real network."," - **Durable archive (2026-10-14):** `scripts/backup-cuore-state.ps1` is the incremental, append-only, sha256-dedup backup for both `C:\\ProgramData\\cuore` (-> `docs/vehicles/<VIN>/state-backup/<date>/`) and Claude Code session data -- transcripts, every `tasks\\*.output` agent transcript, and scratchpad screenshots/html/json (-> `docs/sessions/raw/<date>/<session-id>/`), regenerating `docs/sessions/<date>-agent-discoveries.md` for any session with new agent output; `scripts/save-session-artifacts.ps1` does the same for one named session id. Nothing already written is ever deleted or overwritten -- a file whose sha256 matches its last capture is just marked `skipped-unchanged`, not recopied. Secrets (`sk-ant-*`, `AKIA*`, `\"password\": \"...\"`) are redacted wherever text is copied or digested, even inside a gzipped (>5MB) file -- see `scripts/_backup-common.ps1`. `scripts/hooks/pre-push` is the versioned source for a git `pre-push` hook that runs this archive before every push; **it is not installed** (an automated installer for it was refused by the permission classifier as unauthorized persistence) -- the owner installs it by hand, once per clone: `Copy-Item scripts\\hooks\\pre-push .git\\hooks\\pre-push`. Because git fixes the set of commits a push will send *before* `pre-push` runs, a commit the hook makes is never part of that same push -- by design the hook aborts (exit 1) and asks for a plain `git push github main` re-run to pick it up; the archive step's own failures never block a push (logged to `docs/sessions/archive-errors.log`, hook exits 0).","+- **Pre-push hook install (2026-10-14):** `scripts/hooks/pre-push` is the versioned source; **not auto-installed**. The owner copies it to `.git/hooks/pre-push` once per clone (PowerShell: `Copy-Item scripts\\hooks\\pre-push .git\\hooks\\pre-push`). The hook runs `scripts/backup-cuore-state.ps1` before every push; if the archive creates a new commit, the hook aborts (exit 1) so a re-run of `git push github main` picks it up. Archive failures are logged, never block the push (exit 0).","+- **Rate-limit gotcha (2026-10-14):** Agent sessions hit session-limit throttling mid-work (token exhaustion, not a crash). On limit hit, triage uncommitted files immediately: `git status` shows what's staged/unstaged; if work is half-done, stash (`git stash -u`) and note the stash name so you can resume in a fresh session. Session logs live in `docs/sessions/raw/`.","+- **Date-drift test rule (2026-10-14):** Tests that read CUORE state must isolate `CUORE_STATE_DIR` to a temp dir (set before importing cuore packages). Never assume `\"latest\"` timestamp from the live corpus -- a test that checks `mtime` is brittle against a system clock skew or concurrent writes. Example: `cuore/tests/check_*.py` set `MES_LOG_DIR` before importing, `check_scanlog_page.py` uses a fixture for `observations.jsonl`.","+- **Font and palette rule (2026-10-14):** Marque-specific typefaces (Alfa typeface for Alfa sites) and true-black text (`#000000`, never grey headings or \"adaptive\" dark-mode greys) are design principles, never swapped. Light/dark mode toggles the background and borders, but text weight/face and black remain constant across themes."]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\docs\\handbook\\05-methods-and-gotchas.md"],"shared":true}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"7a6ba059-372f-468a-bd71-3f95d27311d7","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","platform":"windows"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e10386f4-bdaf-4187-88b1-ee8b5672afc7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
