{"parentUuid":"44f33c86-2bde-445a-9c41-e98e27d5345e","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a09009e70701a4229","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cg2UdhuNioU185i3EArjt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SAY1SnhBhsQd9dTBa9AWW9","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd C:/Users/User/mcp-servers && git add cuore/web/static/cuore.css\ngit commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nFix CSS comment-closing typo that silently dropped the whole foundation :root block in real browsers\n\nThe typography pass (ed31772) wrote \"--space-*/--fam-*\" inside a prose\ncomment; the literal \"*/\" there closed the comment early, so every real\nCSS parser (verified via headless Edge CDP, not just the repo's regex-\nbased checks) read the rest of that comment's prose as garbage CSS and\ndiscarded the entire :root { ... } foundation block through its closing\nbrace -- --bg, --ink, --sans, --mono, --fs-*, --fw-*, --accent, --sev-*\nall undefined. Under the OS/browser's light preference this was masked\nby the separate, well-formed `@media (prefers-color-scheme: light)`\nblock; under dark preference (the default, no data-theme set) the page\nfell back to transparent background, Times New Roman, 16px, weight 400\n-- this is the \"visible difference\" from before the pass. Confirmed via\na two-server A/B (this commit vs b87ecfe, the true last pre-pass commit)\nrendered at 768x1024 under both emulated color schemes: after the fix,\nbody background, --bg resolution, hero/heading font-family/weight/size\nand chip styling are now identical between the two again.\n\nOne character fixed (space inserted: \"--space-* / --fam-*\"). Previous\ncommit's font-weight 300 restoration on hero/display elements stands.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\n)\" 2>&1 | tail -10"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":345,"cache_rea